{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A global event bus skips prop drilling but makes bugs harder to trace — any component can emit or listen to an event, and the code doesn't show you which one is which.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Before putting state on a bus, ask if one component should own it. If yes, use props or context with a single write path, not a bus.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Reserve a global bus for genuinely cross-cutting concerns with no single owner. For everything else, keep a typed event map and a discoverable emitter/listener registry if you must use one at all.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
